-- title:
--   Galois invariance of node-local elements with rational coefficients
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$ and let $\mathrm{red} \colon A \to k$ be a ring homomorphism; fix $a \in k$ and an automorphism $\sigma$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over $\mathbb Q$. Let $g$ be an element of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)`, the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathfrak q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the coefficientwise image of `modularFunctionFieldFull (1 * q)`, the latter being the subfield of $\mathbb Q((\mathfrak q))$ generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb Q\,d\,j_{\mathfrak q}$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $1 \cdot q$. Assume that the Laurent series underlying $g$ lies in `modularLocalizedAtPoint (1 * q) (coeffSubring A ⊥) (redRestrict red ⊥) a (a ^ q)`: there are two-variable polynomials $r, s$ with coefficients in $\mathrm{coeffSubring}\,A\,\bot = A \cap \bot$, the intersection of $A$ with the bottom intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$, such that the image of $s$ under `pointEval` at $(a, a^q)$, coefficients reduced by $\mathrm{red}$ along the inclusion $A \cap \bot \subseteq A$, is nonzero in $k$, and such that $g \cdot \mathrm{modularEval}(s) = \mathrm{modularEval}(r)$, where `modularEval` sends the two variables to the $\mathfrak q$-expansions `jqModC` and `jqNModC` of level $1 \cdot q$ and the coefficients to constant series. Then the action of `arithmeticGalois (modularFunctionFieldFull (1 * q)) σ`, the semilinear automorphism applying $\sigma$ to each Laurent coefficient, fixes $g$.
--
--   The statement records that an element of the function field of $X_0(q)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ which is expressible as a quotient of polynomials in $(j, j_q)$ with coefficients in $A \cap \mathbb Q$, with denominator not vanishing at the point $(a, a^q)$ of the special fibre, already has rational $\mathfrak q$-expansion coefficients and is therefore invariant under the arithmetic (coefficientwise) Galois action. It serves the construction of good representatives in the node-descent analysis, being used by [`ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.LevelOneProlongationPair.exists_goodRep_admissible_smul_single_sub_self_of_eq_zero_or_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.PlaceSpecialization.LevelOneProlongationPair.exists_goodRep_admissible_smul_single_sub_self_of_eq_zero_or_eq).
